WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.300
A stain shows what a cell is now.

2
00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.440
It cannot follow descendants.

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.540
A birth date marks one cohort of cells.

4
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:18.220
A lineage is one family: all the descendants of one cell.

5
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:25.120
Could one embryonic cell make many cell types, or did the population hold many

6
00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:29.020
committed ones? Population grafts could not tell.

7
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.720
One route is to watch.

8
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:37.520
Brenner chose a small transparent worm whose cells could be watched alive.

9
00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:43.240
Sulston watched living worms and recorded which cell divided into which.

10
00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:48.420
Another is to inject a tracer into one identified cell.

11
00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.560
Its descendants receive it in active form.

12
00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:57.820
A large dextran tracer cannot pass to neighbours, so only descendants carry it.

13
00:00:58.533 --> 00:01:05.333
A retrovirus joins its genome to a dividing cell's DNA, so every descendant inherits

14
00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:11.493
the insert. A Cre reporter puts a fluorescent protein gene behind a stop flanked by

15
00:01:11.493 --> 00:01:17.673
loxP sites. Cre deletes the stop, so the reporter is read in that cell and all

16
00:01:17.673 --> 00:01:23.793
its descendants. Fuse Cre to a mutated estrogen receptor domain, and tamoxifen

17
00:01:23.793 --> 00:01:28.133
switches it on. A low dose marks few, scattered cells.

18
00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:31.347
Colour can separate neighbours.

19
00:01:32.427 --> 00:01:37.507
Brainbow chooses at random among three or more fluorescent proteins, and

20
00:01:37.507 --> 00:01:41.607
combinations from tandem copies gave about 90 colours.

21
00:01:42.547 --> 00:01:47.667
Confetti switches on one of four, so neighbouring clones can differ in colour.

22
00:01:48.987 --> 00:01:54.467
Weinreb and colleagues gave blood progenitors barcodes expressed as RNA and passed

23
00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:55.727
to every descendant.

24
00:01:56.947 --> 00:02:02.467
McKenna and colleagues used Cas9 target arrays that gather mutations, so shared

25
00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:04.267
patterns reveal relatedness.

26
00:02:05.017 --> 00:02:10.257
Mark cells sparsely, and a cluster is read as one progenitor's family.

27
00:02:10.737 --> 00:02:13.677
That is a sampling argument, not an observation.

28
00:02:14.677 --> 00:02:17.857
In the gut, Snippert and colleagues used four colours.

29
00:02:18.617 --> 00:02:23.917
Some clones grew while others vanished, and crypts drifted toward one colour over

30
00:02:23.917 --> 00:02:25.157
one to six months.

31
00:02:25.797 --> 00:02:29.097
This fits neutral drift among equivalent stem cells.

32
00:02:29.097 --> 00:02:35.157
With N of them, one clone takes over a crypt with probability 1/N.

33
00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:42.190
Two neighbouring cells marked at once look like one clone, so keep induction sparse

34
00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:44.310
and count close pairs of marks.

35
00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:52.570
Leaky labelling: in the 1996 test no excision appeared in untreated animals, yet a

36
00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:58.630
2020 mouse study found labelling without tamoxifen in every CreERT2 line it

37
00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:01.230
examined, more with some reporters than others.

38
00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:06.210
So give full-genotype animals vehicle, and check the reporter stays off.

39
00:03:07.033 --> 00:03:14.953
In 1988, Bronner-Fraser and Fraser injected dye into single chick dorsal neural tube

40
00:03:14.953 --> 00:03:21.273
cells. Many clones held several cell types, so some crest cells are multipotent

41
00:03:21.273 --> 00:03:22.753
before leaving the tube.

42
00:03:23.233 --> 00:03:25.393
That needed single-cell marking.

43
00:03:26.473 --> 00:03:30.453
In 2010, Ginhoux and colleagues pulsed tamoxifen.

44
00:03:30.453 --> 00:03:36.833
Adult mouse microglia derive from primitive myeloid progenitors that arise before

45
00:03:36.833 --> 00:03:41.533
embryonic day 8, not significantly from postnatal blood progenitors.

46
00:03:42.073 --> 00:03:44.093
That needed a pulse in time.

47
00:03:44.967 --> 00:03:51.907
In 2019, Shi and colleagues marked scattered cambium cells in Arabidopsis, using

48
00:03:51.907 --> 00:03:55.207
dexamethasone as the inducer, not tamoxifen.

49
00:03:56.427 --> 00:04:02.687
Of 99 clones at 10 days, 35 spanned xylem, cambium and phloem.

50
00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:07.167
This is read as support for one bifacial stem cell.

51
00:04:08.107 --> 00:04:12.827
A cluster read as one family is a sampling argument, not an observation.
